[{:db/id "2a6c0a49-01f3-50ea-b745-5a7c5cfa9970" :answer/id #uuid "2a6c0a49-01f3-50ea-b745-5a7c5cfa9970" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2e012937-cb75-5afb-b9ca-7b669b2673ba" :answer/id #uuid "2e012937-cb75-5afb-b9ca-7b669b2673ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "603d58c2-77dc-53d3-835f-ca352ce1e392" :answer/id #uuid "603d58c2-77dc-53d3-835f-ca352ce1e392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ec567be1-2042-5aa0-a72f-b2a7a1771cbe" :answer/id #uuid "ec567be1-2042-5aa0-a72f-b2a7a1771cbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0bde0c95-87d9-5021-b422-7d119cac0a2f" :answer/id #uuid "0bde0c95-87d9-5021-b422-7d119cac0a2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "690d18f9-3146-524d-a5a2-208e9362d1d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "690d18f9-3146-524d-a5a2-208e9362d1d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["2a6c0a49-01f3-50ea-b745-5a7c5cfa9970" "2e012937-cb75-5afb-b9ca-7b669b2673ba" "603d58c2-77dc-53d3-835f-ca352ce1e392" "ec567be1-2042-5aa0-a72f-b2a7a1771cbe" "0bde0c95-87d9-5021-b422-7d119cac0a2f"] :answer-field/correct "ec567be1-2042-5aa0-a72f-b2a7a1771cbe" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "42a708f1-2e3f-5710-8d8f-00feeafdf2b2" :question/id #uuid "42a708f1-2e3f-5710-8d8f-00feeafdf2b2" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n$y = \\frac{1}{x}, y = \\frac{4}{x}, y = 3x, y = 4x$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\nxy=1,\\,xy=4,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=3,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=4\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu=xy,\\,v=\\frac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u=xy$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=1\\,⟹\\,u=1 \\\\  & xy=4\\,⟹\\,u=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=\\frac{y}{x}$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y}{x}=3\\,⟹\\,v=3 \\\\  & \\frac{y}{x}=4\\,⟹\\,v=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,3\\le v\\le 4\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/88/88750e49134feaa087b1f48ddee12faeb30ca8a31dd3b5bebb989f4c7c891ae7.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -\\frac{y}{x^2} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (4-1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["690d18f9-3146-524d-a5a2-208e9362d1d6"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "c8dd696a-a439-5722-8165-12e98bab773e" :answer/id #uuid "c8dd696a-a439-5722-8165-12e98bab773e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4bc03413-e383-5579-b76c-092cfdf0ba2d" :answer/id #uuid "4bc03413-e383-5579-b76c-092cfdf0ba2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f0551450-197d-58b1-8016-b5ae5d19fb42" :answer/id #uuid "f0551450-197d-58b1-8016-b5ae5d19fb42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cf207c00-d6db-5ca5-ae88-332c78997858" :answer/id #uuid "cf207c00-d6db-5ca5-ae88-332c78997858" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9cf1d1bd-cd3b-5362-a201-96e2f8d65215" :answer/id #uuid "9cf1d1bd-cd3b-5362-a201-96e2f8d65215" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b06b705a-a49e-57b4-8e75-93b51d1cd651" :answer-field/id #uuid "b06b705a-a49e-57b4-8e75-93b51d1cd651" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["c8dd696a-a439-5722-8165-12e98bab773e" "4bc03413-e383-5579-b76c-092cfdf0ba2d" "f0551450-197d-58b1-8016-b5ae5d19fb42" "cf207c00-d6db-5ca5-ae88-332c78997858" "9cf1d1bd-cd3b-5362-a201-96e2f8d65215"] :answer-field/correct "c8dd696a-a439-5722-8165-12e98bab773e" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "122c57cf-cfe9-5e24-b30b-49b9810a796b" :question/id #uuid "122c57cf-cfe9-5e24-b30b-49b9810a796b" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n$y = \\frac{3}{x}, y = \\frac{7}{x}, y = 4x, y = 5x$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\nxy=3,\\,xy=7,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=4,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=5\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu=xy,\\,v=\\frac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u=xy$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=3\\,⟹\\,u=3 \\\\  & xy=7\\,⟹\\,u=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=\\frac{y}{x}$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y}{x}=4\\,⟹\\,v=4 \\\\  & \\frac{y}{x}=5\\,⟹\\,v=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,3\\le u\\le 7,\\,4\\le v\\le 5\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/3d/3dc524083463c8c370ff1f79d68093f0d3f2c2fe1ceb5cd47824782e35a0bac9.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -\\frac{y}{x^2} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{4}^{5}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (7-3)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["b06b705a-a49e-57b4-8e75-93b51d1cd651"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d5935ed1-7de1-54f7-8776-fa2897e513ea" :answer/id #uuid "d5935ed1-7de1-54f7-8776-fa2897e513ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b8309c86-ea8f-5023-84d6-cc1e1d1ff7de" :answer/id #uuid "b8309c86-ea8f-5023-84d6-cc1e1d1ff7de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b146b24c-8adf-51d6-9b4a-ace2765fa126" :answer/id #uuid "b146b24c-8adf-51d6-9b4a-ace2765fa126" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fe94daf5-1f4e-5c5e-a0ad-b319ec84510e" :answer/id #uuid "fe94daf5-1f4e-5c5e-a0ad-b319ec84510e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7679f101-3932-576a-bb5f-e5c4e0d8f328" :answer/id #uuid "7679f101-3932-576a-bb5f-e5c4e0d8f328" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7b4bdfb4-f617-5835-a9b7-bf4aa30c0245" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b4bdfb4-f617-5835-a9b7-bf4aa30c0245" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d5935ed1-7de1-54f7-8776-fa2897e513ea" "b8309c86-ea8f-5023-84d6-cc1e1d1ff7de" "b146b24c-8adf-51d6-9b4a-ace2765fa126" "fe94daf5-1f4e-5c5e-a0ad-b319ec84510e" "7679f101-3932-576a-bb5f-e5c4e0d8f328"] :answer-field/correct "d5935ed1-7de1-54f7-8776-fa2897e513ea" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "1e54c2fb-3e60-532d-b51f-b6a974c7d6cf" :question/id #uuid "1e54c2fb-3e60-532d-b51f-b6a974c7d6cf" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n$y = \\frac{2}{x}, y = \\frac{5}{x}, y = 2x, y = 3x$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\nxy=2,\\,xy=5,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=2,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=3\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu=xy,\\,v=\\frac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u=xy$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=2\\,⟹\\,u=2 \\\\  & xy=5\\,⟹\\,u=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=\\frac{y}{x}$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y}{x}=2\\,⟹\\,v=2 \\\\  & \\frac{y}{x}=3\\,⟹\\,v=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 5,\\,2\\le v\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/2c/2cdd0431c256b72ded23c14fac4098b518a46603d46d5dfd238c54b3a46c66db.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -\\frac{y}{x^2} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (5-2)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["7b4bdfb4-f617-5835-a9b7-bf4aa30c0245"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "b0c76cd2-18bc-54c4-bec6-41c9e208d51b" :answer/id #uuid "b0c76cd2-18bc-54c4-bec6-41c9e208d51b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3f03a8f3-09d3-5671-890f-62e7bfebe2dd" :answer/id #uuid "3f03a8f3-09d3-5671-890f-62e7bfebe2dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f72a6040-f6eb-5203-b778-5f0e5d0eb63b" :answer/id #uuid "f72a6040-f6eb-5203-b778-5f0e5d0eb63b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6a93d690-2db3-54db-8e20-261a49e04fed" :answer/id #uuid "6a93d690-2db3-54db-8e20-261a49e04fed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e5ff2435-f7c2-57f1-a4e1-b9ad0070da42" :answer/id #uuid "e5ff2435-f7c2-57f1-a4e1-b9ad0070da42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "18f802c8-f27c-572f-a462-5834e5ade5cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "18f802c8-f27c-572f-a462-5834e5ade5cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["b0c76cd2-18bc-54c4-bec6-41c9e208d51b" "3f03a8f3-09d3-5671-890f-62e7bfebe2dd" "f72a6040-f6eb-5203-b778-5f0e5d0eb63b" "6a93d690-2db3-54db-8e20-261a49e04fed" "e5ff2435-f7c2-57f1-a4e1-b9ad0070da42"] :answer-field/correct "f72a6040-f6eb-5203-b778-5f0e5d0eb63b" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "df897641-0828-516d-b42d-f7e72c630377" :question/id #uuid "df897641-0828-516d-b42d-f7e72c630377" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n$y = \\frac{3}{x}, y = \\frac{7}{x}, y = 3x, y = 5x$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\nxy=3,\\,xy=7,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=3,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=5\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu=xy,\\,v=\\frac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u=xy$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=3\\,⟹\\,u=3 \\\\  & xy=7\\,⟹\\,u=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=\\frac{y}{x}$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y}{x}=3\\,⟹\\,v=3 \\\\  & \\frac{y}{x}=5\\,⟹\\,v=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,3\\le u\\le 7,\\,3\\le v\\le 5\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/cf/cf598751d1bb1edda1bb65fd5b94d2ad5805289c48716f69a71394fd3684e920.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -\\frac{y}{x^2} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{3}^{7}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (7-3)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["18f802c8-f27c-572f-a462-5834e5ade5cc"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "12fb765d-ae64-5832-b007-b74f3340d57d" :answer/id #uuid "12fb765d-ae64-5832-b007-b74f3340d57d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fe95aa6e-580a-552f-be09-ab51db51fae9" :answer/id #uuid "fe95aa6e-580a-552f-be09-ab51db51fae9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f8b850bc-8ee1-5ce0-802a-5fddf2d584a1" :answer/id #uuid "f8b850bc-8ee1-5ce0-802a-5fddf2d584a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9945870d-1803-5fe4-9bf3-865f89d3cd0d" :answer/id #uuid "9945870d-1803-5fe4-9bf3-865f89d3cd0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "62aef600-0c78-54d8-81c7-8d4524fdf63c" :answer/id #uuid "62aef600-0c78-54d8-81c7-8d4524fdf63c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b1862914-74d2-5d9e-9a9b-863b6c76ac81" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1862914-74d2-5d9e-9a9b-863b6c76ac81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["12fb765d-ae64-5832-b007-b74f3340d57d" "fe95aa6e-580a-552f-be09-ab51db51fae9" "f8b850bc-8ee1-5ce0-802a-5fddf2d584a1" "9945870d-1803-5fe4-9bf3-865f89d3cd0d" "62aef600-0c78-54d8-81c7-8d4524fdf63c"] :answer-field/correct "f8b850bc-8ee1-5ce0-802a-5fddf2d584a1" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "7fd0b89a-d3f8-5c0c-990c-72bcaf568dcc" :question/id #uuid "7fd0b89a-d3f8-5c0c-990c-72bcaf568dcc" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n$y = \\frac{4}{x}, y = \\frac{5}{x}, y = 3x, y = 5x$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\nxy=4,\\,xy=5,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=3,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=5\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu=xy,\\,v=\\frac{y}{x}\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u=xy$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=4\\,⟹\\,u=4 \\\\  & xy=5\\,⟹\\,u=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=\\frac{y}{x}$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y}{x}=3\\,⟹\\,v=3 \\\\  & \\frac{y}{x}=5\\,⟹\\,v=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,4\\le u\\le 5,\\,3\\le v\\le 5\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/56/560d4d074d9d07eb034d92b8f1dfabfc3e59d659c91d80c3fedf68367a575e41.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -\\frac{y}{x^2} & \\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}+\\frac{y}{x} \\\\  & =2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (5-4)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["b1862914-74d2-5d9e-9a9b-863b6c76ac81"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "9b26d1d3-5a01-5340-ac5c-0ff36304fe94" :answer/id #uuid "9b26d1d3-5a01-5340-ac5c-0ff36304fe94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "efd43ec0-cf88-554f-b689-3c042afa4eca" :answer/id #uuid "efd43ec0-cf88-554f-b689-3c042afa4eca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8d01b629-0fe6-5f74-a3c7-5fb63d97ee92" :answer/id #uuid "8d01b629-0fe6-5f74-a3c7-5fb63d97ee92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "615769bf-cd9e-5b6c-bdf0-52ec2d404c73" :answer/id #uuid "615769bf-cd9e-5b6c-bdf0-52ec2d404c73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d4ee7848-ffd6-5369-a172-3a5c72a7a437" :answer/id #uuid "d4ee7848-ffd6-5369-a172-3a5c72a7a437" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5a1ce500-1558-50c5-bb88-90956f218df6" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1ce500-1558-50c5-bb88-90956f218df6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["9b26d1d3-5a01-5340-ac5c-0ff36304fe94" "efd43ec0-cf88-554f-b689-3c042afa4eca" "8d01b629-0fe6-5f74-a3c7-5fb63d97ee92" "615769bf-cd9e-5b6c-bdf0-52ec2d404c73" "d4ee7848-ffd6-5369-a172-3a5c72a7a437"] :answer-field/correct "8d01b629-0fe6-5f74-a3c7-5fb63d97ee92" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "771d8ee7-1782-5b04-8868-20616e0c6e6f" :question/id #uuid "771d8ee7-1782-5b04-8868-20616e0c6e6f" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}},\\,y=\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}},\\,y=\\frac{2}{x},\\,y=\\frac{6}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}y=3,\\,{x}^{2}y=6,\\,xy=2,\\,xy=6\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}y,\\,v=xy\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u={x}^{2}y$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2}y=3\\,⟹\\,u=3 \\\\  & {x}^{2}y=6\\,⟹\\,u=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=xy$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=2\\,⟹\\,v=2 \\\\  & xy=6\\,⟹\\,v=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,3\\le u\\le 6,\\,2\\le v\\le 6\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/a4/a42d50fe797c9450b27acde75ac7b69ed3e4ea5acc6c9dc93cd6df18b9ed1882.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ y & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{1}{u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)\\cdot (6-2) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["5a1ce500-1558-50c5-bb88-90956f218df6"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "210c7817-face-512a-bd86-a64b17d52373" :answer/id #uuid "210c7817-face-512a-bd86-a64b17d52373" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "254ec97c-0212-583c-b49e-6a869eb1d355" :answer/id #uuid "254ec97c-0212-583c-b49e-6a869eb1d355" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cdcb6add-4b39-5487-9f4a-cb645e09e337" :answer/id #uuid "cdcb6add-4b39-5487-9f4a-cb645e09e337" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "69982d7e-1d88-5550-9f63-20d44a587a81" :answer/id #uuid "69982d7e-1d88-5550-9f63-20d44a587a81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f95423eb-63d2-501d-87fa-8c0d6bc4a077" :answer/id #uuid "f95423eb-63d2-501d-87fa-8c0d6bc4a077" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2a292981-3f43-5a33-b54f-0f6a73d0854d" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a292981-3f43-5a33-b54f-0f6a73d0854d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["210c7817-face-512a-bd86-a64b17d52373" "254ec97c-0212-583c-b49e-6a869eb1d355" "cdcb6add-4b39-5487-9f4a-cb645e09e337" "69982d7e-1d88-5550-9f63-20d44a587a81" "f95423eb-63d2-501d-87fa-8c0d6bc4a077"] :answer-field/correct "cdcb6add-4b39-5487-9f4a-cb645e09e337" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "5805f5a4-c211-580d-a915-dc2770c526f8" :question/id #uuid "5805f5a4-c211-580d-a915-dc2770c526f8" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}},\\,y=\\frac{7}{{x}^{2}},\\,y=\\frac{4}{x},\\,y=\\frac{8}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}y=4,\\,{x}^{2}y=7,\\,xy=4,\\,xy=8\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu={x}^{2}y,\\,v=xy\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u={x}^{2}y$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2}y=4\\,⟹\\,u=4 \\\\  & {x}^{2}y=7\\,⟹\\,u=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=xy$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=4\\,⟹\\,v=4 \\\\  & xy=8\\,⟹\\,v=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,4\\le u\\le 7,\\,4\\le v\\le 8\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/47/475635e9575bd2f30069f2ee5f3b29bd6d7bf47db0cb6d5a96f981e36b8117c6.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2xy & {x}^{2} \\\\ y & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y-{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{u}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{1}{u}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{7}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{4}^{8}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)\\cdot (8-4) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["2a292981-3f43-5a33-b54f-0f6a73d0854d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "7c271fcc-050b-5bd7-bb0a-bd7e59bd8013" :answer/id #uuid "7c271fcc-050b-5bd7-bb0a-bd7e59bd8013" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ee8c388f-4bcc-5ca9-9c82-9cdfdfa398e7" :answer/id #uuid "ee8c388f-4bcc-5ca9-9c82-9cdfdfa398e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fb51af7c-e436-58e4-828c-830ac59f2a0c" :answer/id #uuid "fb51af7c-e436-58e4-828c-830ac59f2a0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "73eb65d7-09df-500e-9d56-1a66efa416ec" :answer/id #uuid "73eb65d7-09df-500e-9d56-1a66efa416ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "abbdfe07-8aed-512d-9ff0-01181e26a377" :answer/id #uuid "abbdfe07-8aed-512d-9ff0-01181e26a377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fe81a033-5b30-59ce-b828-9ec0ad8c66db" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe81a033-5b30-59ce-b828-9ec0ad8c66db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["7c271fcc-050b-5bd7-bb0a-bd7e59bd8013" "ee8c388f-4bcc-5ca9-9c82-9cdfdfa398e7" "fb51af7c-e436-58e4-828c-830ac59f2a0c" "73eb65d7-09df-500e-9d56-1a66efa416ec" "abbdfe07-8aed-512d-9ff0-01181e26a377"] :answer-field/correct "7c271fcc-050b-5bd7-bb0a-bd7e59bd8013" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "21d697ec-a429-5e49-b479-9da388eda962" :question/id #uuid "21d697ec-a429-5e49-b479-9da388eda962" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{x},\\,y=\\frac{5}{x},\\,x=2{y}^{2},\\,x=3{y}^{2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\nxy=2,\\,xy=5,\\,\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}=2,\\,\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}=3\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu=xy,\\,v=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u=xy$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=2\\,⟹\\,u=2 \\\\  & xy=5\\,⟹\\,u=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}=2\\,⟹\\,v=2 \\\\  & \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}=3\\,⟹\\,v=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,2\\le u\\le 5,\\,2\\le v\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\n![](images/2c/2cdd0431c256b72ded23c14fac4098b518a46603d46d5dfd238c54b3a46c66db.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} & -\\frac{2x}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}|-\\frac{1}{3v}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (5-2)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["fe81a033-5b30-59ce-b828-9ec0ad8c66db"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "d05330ff-0fe3-5718-b0f5-bbdce66c8438" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186129262.py"} [:db/add 17592186129262 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186129262 :knowledge-point/questions ["42a708f1-2e3f-5710-8d8f-00feeafdf2b2" "122c57cf-cfe9-5e24-b30b-49b9810a796b" "1e54c2fb-3e60-532d-b51f-b6a974c7d6cf" "df897641-0828-516d-b42d-f7e72c630377" "7fd0b89a-d3f8-5c0c-990c-72bcaf568dcc" "771d8ee7-1782-5b04-8868-20616e0c6e6f" "5805f5a4-c211-580d-a915-dc2770c526f8" "21d697ec-a429-5e49-b479-9da388eda962"]} [:db/ensure 17592186129262 :knowledge-point/validate]]
